  "notes": "Refers to financial support provided by governments, organizations, or foundations to promote research, arts, social welfare, or other public-interest activities. The word emphasizes the supportive and promotional aspect of the funding.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {助成金|じょせいきん}: subsidy, grant money\n- {助成|じょせい}{制度|せいど}: subsidy system\n- {助成|じょせい}を{受|う}ける: to receive a subsidy\n- {助成|じょせい}{事業|じぎょう}: subsidized project\n- {助成|じょせい}{団体|だんたい}: grant-giving organization\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {補助|ほじょ}: assistance, supplement — broader meaning; {補助金|ほじょきん} is often interchangeable with {助成金|じょせいきん}\n- {援助|えんじょ}: aid, support — more general, includes non-financial help\n- {支援|しえん}: support — broader and more commonly used in everyday contexts\n- {交付|こうふ}: disbursement, granting — focuses on the act of distributing funds",
